  "body": "Found by a Windows 11 sanity check of the v0.23.0 zip (Parallels ARM64 VM): `camcraft-cli process examples/first-part.camproj` exits 0 (3 ops, no warnings) and writes 369 lines / 9531 bytes with the Fanuc post. The shipped `examples/first-part.nc` has 281 lines / 5963 bytes.\n\nThe shipped file is from the commit that added the example (993a241b0, #291). Since then the post output gained `G21` and a rapid approach to clearance (`G00 Z45.`) before the first cut; the shipped file starts cutting with `G01 X-55 Y-25 Z15 F300` straight after `M8`. A user who compares their output with the example sees a different program and cannot tell which is right.\n\n`examples/first-4axis-part.nc` matches byte for byte, because a test pins it (`first_4axis_part`). `first-part.nc` has no such pin.\n\nDone means: `examples/first-part.nc` regenerated from `first-part.camproj` with the current program, and a test that fails when they drift apart (the `first_4axis_part` pattern); `first-router-part` gets a shipped `.nc` and the same pin, or the guide says why it has none.\n",
